> AMENDED 2026-10-31 (operator): the "node host shell" below reads as shared CAP-STACK stages behind capability-named ports (browser vessels use these caps and may take a node-like role). Only substrate bindings (thread kind, store kind, socket server) stay per-host. C5 cuts a capability shell, never a node shell; C6 carries R1-R19 stages too.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/god-method-lift-map-preparenodebooton`>>

! God-method lift map: prepareNodeBootOn (open-node-vessel.ts:709-3546)
Lift-Seer (cold Opus reader), 2026-10-31. Read-only skim; line ranges hold, per-stage claims rest on excerpts. Written to disk by the controller (subagent write refused).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/tl-dr`>>

!! TL;DR
# The function fuses two jobs: a NODE HOST SHELL (R1-R19: Repo, WS face-gates, share verdict, membership/antigen/edge-shadow holders, dials, relays) and a VesselOrchestration FACTORY (R22-R35: keel, wikiSlot, openDaemon, wireVerbs, afterDaemon, makePool, afterLive). The shared composeCoreVessel (lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts:51) already sequences that contract for both vessels: the seam exists.
# Hidden shared state: ~40 forward-declared lets (share policy 997-1021 reads 15); `let x!` boot cells (1697-1795); four process-global doors in worker-handle.ts (setRestDoor/setCasDoor/setDyadDoor/setCustodyWriteDoor): two vessels in one process clobber each other's doors, which is why tests enter only through a whole boot.
# VM lifts stay narrow. TS->TW5 already works: plugin-build/ compiles any TS with a /*\ module-type \*/ header to CJS (46 modules ship so). The *-vm startup modules (worldline-read-vm.ts, query-derive-vm.ts) set the pattern: host ships data in, VM computes. Candidates: verb-provider math (2690-3036: computeMismatch, signalOrExtract, couple/crystallizeSignal) and wireVerbs' wiki-act slot routing. NEVER: transport/custody/keys (R10, R15, R24, R29, R30, rekey/cad-seal verbs). Syncadaptor/saver ruled out (glass mirror censusPreloads refuses; bootTrustedModules admits only library). MIRROR HAZARD: shared-plugin code loads in the mirror too; custody-adjacent VM code rides a daemon-only plugin chosen by recipe in resolveNodeIslandPluginCids (2569).
# The bigger win: pure modules + shared isomorphic stages. open-browser-vessel.ts bootUnderLock (490-1887) hand-repeats island resolution (584), climb (649), dyads (858), catalog (928), residency (950), PersonaGroup ring (1456), sibling channel (1488), wiki-switch/persona/face verbs (1521-1736), founding/admit.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/substrate`>>

!! Substrate
Node host shell -> composeCoreVessel -> openDaemonVmCore -> worker_threads daemon island (node-daemon-island.ts -> runSovereignKernel -> TW5Engine.boot). The island holds the face-atom seed (daemonAuth), Keyhive, sealed store; asks host for rest/cas/dyad/custody-write over its port. VesselIslandPool spawns one worker per wiki. Browser vessel Worker/SharedWorker runs the same kernel over IDB/OPFS. Page mirror (glass-mirror.ts:46) boots one guarded engine behind MIRROR_TOKEN, no syncer, fed by the port alone.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ranked-cuts`>>

!! Ranked cuts (each red-first)
# C1 doors instance-owned: one VesselDoors object into nodeWorkerHandle. HOST, S. Red: two handles answer distinct asks. WAITS u1.
# C2 BootCells: typed cells replacing `let x!`, refusing read-before-set by name. S.
# C3 ShareInputs: one cell feeding the already-pure selfSlotShareDecision; decision-table tests. WAITS ralias.
# C4 pure readers: bootstrap parse + torn-face check (1868-1905), daemonAuth builder (2527-2566), diskMirrorGrant (3332), boot pin list (3247), postureOf/contractHolds/gateNexuses, wiki-act routing, backupDoor's three cloned askIslandMemory getters (3478-3540, delete dup). R23/R30/R35/R36 touched by no lane: can start now.
# C5 split host shell from orchestration -> node-orchestration.ts (NodeShell port + cells); characterization tests first.
# C6 shared isomorphic stages, one stage per PR into mesh (transport-free) or tw5 (keel), deleting the browser twin in the same PR; ports named by capability, never host.
# C7 verb math -> daemon-only *-vm startup module; py/fs pipe stays host.
# Deletion candidates: peerContractNymMap (875, nothing fills it; surface to operator), "bridge until O1" catalogForViews (863).
C1-C4 open seams, no behavior change, can land before the founding; C5-C7 ride the stage-cut.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/laws`>>

!! Laws
No key on a surface blocks VM lifts of R10, R15, R22 systemCanon, R24, R29, R30, R33. One owner per registry: global doors break it per process; C1 cures. No global now: the pool's mountSilenceMs/mountStallMs should arrive as injected deadlines. Sovereign-worker primacy (functor-discipline.mem#/sovereign-worker) argues for C7.

<<~/ahu>>

